  "solution": {
    "approach": "The program does not need to read any data. It simply prints four rows, each consisting of four asterisk characters. A dummy test case count T=1 is used so that the code follows the common template of looping over test cases.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) – constant work to output 16 characters.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) – only a few loop counters.",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main(){int T=1;for(int t=0;t<T;++t){for(int i=0;i<4;++i){for(int j=0;j<4;++j)putchar('*');putchar('\\n');}}return 0;}",
      "C++": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int T=1;for(int t=0;t<T;++t){for(int i=0;i<4;++i){for(int j=0;j<4;++j)cout<<'*';cout<<'\\n';}}return 0;}",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main{public static void main(String[] args)throws Exception{int T=1;StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();for(int t=0;t<T;++t){for(int i=0;i<4;++i){sb.append(\"****\");sb.append('\\n');}}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "def main():\n    T=1\n    for _ in range(T):\n        for _ in range(4):\n            print('*'*4)\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    main()",
      "JavaScript": "const fs=require('fs');\nfs.readFileSync(0,'utf8');\nlet T=1;\nlet out=[];\nfor(let t=0;t<T;++t){\n  for(let i=0;i<4;++i){out.push('****');}\n}\nconsole.log(out.join('\\n'));"
    },
